course: dictionary
lesson: 8108
title: Giving things up with renounce
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To renounce something means to give it up, often in a formal or public way. People can renounce a right, a title, a claim, or a belief. Look at the words around it to find the clues.
explain: «Whoever conceals their sins does not prosper, but the one who confesses and renounces them finds mercy.» The words confesses and renounces are joined together, so they must be doing a similar job. Confessing means telling the truth, so renouncing must mean turning away from something you did wrong.
explain: In history, a king who renounces the throne gives up his right to be king. In the news, a group that renounces violence says it will stop using violence. In a baptism, parents and godparents renounce evil for the child. The thing that is given up always comes right after the word renounce.
fact: Renounce is a verb, so its forms are renounce, renounces, renounced and renouncing.
fact: Renounce means to say officially or publicly that you give up a right, title or claim.
fact: Renounce can also mean to stop believing in or supporting something, as in «renounce violence».
fact: In church, to renounce means to reject evil and sin, as Christians do at a baptism.
fact: «Renounce your citizenship» means officially giving up being a citizen of a country.
exercise: Proverbs says, «Whoever confesses and renounces them finds mercy.» What does renounces mean here? | Hides them from everyone | *Gives up and turns away from them | Counts them carefully | Shouts about them loudly
exercise: In history, a king «renounced the throne». What does that mean? | He sat on it proudly | He built a new one | *He officially gave it up | He painted it gold
exercise: In a story, a hero «renounces riches to help others». What does renounces riches mean? | Asks for more riches | Hides riches under the bed | Counts riches each day | *Gives up riches
test: At a baptism, parents are asked, «Do you renounce evil?» What does renounce mean? | Tell a story about evil | *Reject evil | Ask for more evil
test: «The group will renounce violence.» What does this sentence tell you? | The group will hide its violence | The group will start a fight | The group will ask for violence | *The group will stop supporting violence
exam: Which sentence uses renounce correctly? | The prince renounced a sunny day at the park | The prince renounced the cake before he ate it | *The prince renounced his claim to the crown | The prince renounced his lunch was delicious
